WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.160
It is
a privilege to be a detective.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.440
Mark Birch: You deal with lots
and lots of horrible things,

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:07.560
that comes with the territory.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.200
The majority of us
don't have to see these things,

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.520
don't have to
deal with these things.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.040
The launch of the fifth
murder enquiry in such

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.400
a short space of time ...

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.520
Martin Brunning: Justice for
the victims is absolutely

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.440
the most important thing.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.240
- You've been arrested
on suspicion of attempted

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.760
murder and murder.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.320
- Could be worse.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.280
Officer PTC: We can
only imagine the grief of

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.360
the families who lost
their loved ones in such

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.520
brutal circumstances.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.840
- ... with your DNA.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.440
How can that be?

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.320
- No comment.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.960
Journalist PTC: The judge
said the murder showed a degree

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.680
of premeditation and planning.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:47.960
He'd been stabbed and beaten.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.320
Howard Groves: It was very
much a manhunt at that stage

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.520
of the investigation.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.480
He knew that the
walls were closing in on him.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.640
Stewart Gull: I always remember
a more experienced officer

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.360
telling me, you know, you,
you never forget these jobs,

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.880
and he was right.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:05.240
VO: These are the detectives
who solved some of Britain's

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.760
most notorious homicides.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.360
Now they re-live those cases.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.040
Martin Brunning: Every fear
that I had was being realised

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.520
in front of my eyes.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:20.040
VO: Through every twist and
turn of the investigation ...

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.400
Mark Birch: The only
way you forget about it is ...

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.280
is when you're asleep.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.880
VO: Their personal accounts
reveal what it really takes

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.240
to capture a killer
and bring them to justice.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.280
Howard Groves:
As a detective, you know, there,

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.000
there can't be any
greater honour than for you

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:44.040
to investigate the death- or
murder- of another human being.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:58.920
Mark PTC: Fairly early
in my career I wanted

00:01:59.000 --> 00:01:59.920
to be a detective.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:05.720
I had thirty-one years in
the Police and I became Head

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.000
of CID for a police force.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:13.680
You're entrusted with some
really, really serious stuff.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:20.760
You're trusted by the
public to do the right thing.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.080
Mark: This
was one of the most challenging,

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.960
one of the most difficult
enquiries I've had to deal with.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.040
The level of violence that
was used was beyond anything

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:39.320
I'd ever dealt with before,
so I'll never forget it.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.120
Mark PTC: It started
with a phone call from

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.760
the crime manager at the local
police station at Peterborough.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.120
This guy Andrew Scanlan
had been reported missing

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.640
by his girlfriend
Louise earlier in November,

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.640
and it had been handled as
a Missing From Home enquiry

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.280
since then by a locum officer.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:18.640
VO: When that phone call comes
through to DCS Mark Birch:,

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.360
Andrew's been missing
for five weeks.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:25.240
Unemployed and engaging
in low-level crime,

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:28.400
he was estranged from his
family and living on Dickens

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.400
Street with his girlfriend,
Louise, when he disappeared .

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.480
At first, there was
no particular cause for concern.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.240
Mark PTC: Louise had received
a text message saying 'no need

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.520
to worry, I'm off to London',
or words to that effect.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.360
Given that Andrew Scanlan was an
adult, thirty-five years of age,

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:49.720
adults are allowed
to go missing.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:54.720
Nothing was specifically leaping
out at that stage to say

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.120
that we've got a big problem
here, or there is a problem,

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.720
other than trying to find out
and unearth where he was

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.720
and if he was safe and well.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:05.880
VO: But as police
continue making routine checks,

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.000
they discover a lead.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.280
During the five weeks
Andrew's been gone,

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.880
his bank
card is in regular use.

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:18.280
Not in London, as his
text to his girlfriend suggests,

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.120
but much closer to home.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.240
Mark PTC: It was being
accessed every Friday

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.920
and a hundred and ninety
pounds was being withdrawn.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:31.160
So the Missing From Home
officer set up observations on

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.320
the cashpoint where this hundred
and ninety pounds was being

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:36.280
withdrawn in Peterborough.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.360
Mark PTC: You've got a card
and a bank that suddenly money's

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.240
being withdrawn from,
but it's not being withdrawn

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.920
by Andrew Scanlan.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:50.640
There is something
going on here.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:55.480
VO: Under Mark Birch:'s lead,
what had been a routine Missing

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:59.840
Person's enquiry now becomes
a criminal investigation

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:01.280
of the most serious kind.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:05.120
Mark PTC: Ultimately
I'm responsible for homicides

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.280
in the, in the county.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.360
People talk about gut instinct.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:12.120
The truth of the matter is,
when you look at gut instinct

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.440
it isn't gut instinct, is it?

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.680
It's based around
your own personal experience,

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.320
it's based around the facts
that are put in front

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.600
of you and you make a,
a decision.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:25.840
Having sat down, talked through
all the facts that surrounded

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:30.480
the case, they were all giving
me a feeling that something

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.120
had happened to Andrew Scanlan.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:37.240
VO: Mark Birch: suspects the
very worst - that Andrew is

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:40.520
not missing, but murdered.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:44.040
With no clear evidence beyond
a misused bank card he has

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.960
to make a quick
and difficult decision.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:51.920
Mark PTC: We're now talking
three days before Christmas,

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.840
police officers
are the same as everyone else,

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.400
they've got
families, they've got a life,

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.240
they've got things
that are going on.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.520
These are the sort of things
that were going through my head.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.600
Mark PTC: Don't get me wrong
- it wouldn't matter what time

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.960
of year, what time if day,
if we're talking investigation

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.280
of a murder
it's going to happen.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:19.480
But what you don't want to
do is put the balloon up

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.600
and start a murder
enquiry using a substantial

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:25.360
amount of staff
when you didn't need to.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.000
Especially if it wasn't
a murder enquiry in the end,

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:30.600
if Andrew Scanlan happened
to be living in a flat

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:33.120
in London safe and well.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:42.560
Mark PTC: Every
day matters in a murder enquiry.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.320
Better to make a decision
that's wrong than not make

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.640
a decision at all.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:51.160
There's no doubt in my mind that
this guy has been murdered and

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.200
if we don't pick it up now we're
going to lose more evidence.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:59.800
VO: With his decision
made, DCS Birch escalates

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:03.880
the investigation and builds a
team to work through Christmas.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:09.080
Mark PTC: We've got five
or six weeks of evidence that

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:10.600
potentially could have gone.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.600
And that includes CCTV footage.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:15.000
You know, some,
some cameras they only roll

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.920
on a 24-hour clock.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:18.960
There's the forensic evidence.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.800
Wherever the scene
was, where he was taken from,

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:24.360
where he's been killed,
where he's been deposited,

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.440
there's evidence
there that could be lost.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.320
There's witnesses' evidence.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:33.040
So a witness may remember
something after a day or two.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:37.680
Give them five or six
weeks, it becomes less clear.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:41.680
For me it's now about retrieving
all the evidence I possibly can.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:49.720
Mark PTC: I'm going to
ramp up the number of officers

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.320
Involved in the investigation.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.400
I'm going to ramp up
the techniques that we use

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:57.080
in terms of bringing
in a murder enquiry room,

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.400
which is going
to involve lots of staff,

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:05.960
lots of
time and lots of money.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.840
VO: The first,
and most obvious suspect,

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:14.160
is the man who'd been
using Andrew's bank card-

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:16.520
Peter Cottrell.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:19.480
He's now brought in for
questioning and turns out

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:23.080
to be Andrew's best friend.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:26.440
Peter had no bank account
of his own so Andrew lent

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:32.800
him his card to
pay in and withdraw his wages.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:34.240
Mark PTC: The fact that
the bank account was being

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:38.200
used actually
became a bit of a red herring.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.240
Sometimes you can put a
load of effort into something

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:43.480
and you can work your
socks off, and you'll get to

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:46.040
a place and it's,
it's gone the wrong direction,

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:48.280
that's not the answer.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.960
Now turn away, forget about
it, move on to the next place.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:03.960
VO: Andrew's girlfriend
Louise is also questioned.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:06.960
Together, she and Peter
produce a compelling new lead.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:12.520
On the night Andrew
was last seen, he had a visit.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:17.640
Mark PTC: The version
of events that Peter and Louise

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:21.920
gave us was simply this: so on
the seventeenth of November two

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.160
thousand and six they
get a knock on the door

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.160
and Mark Baigent is at the door.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:28.720
James Baigent
was sitting in the car outside.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:34.720
VO: Mark and James Baigent
are Andrew Scanlan's younger

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:37.280
half-brothers.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:40.600
The three share the same mother,
Linda, who has recently died.

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:47.120
Mark PTC: Mark
Baigent comes into the address,

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:49.720
tells Andrew that as a result
of their mother's death

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:52.880
he's been left a sum of money,
about five thousand pounds,

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:55.040
but that Andrew Scanlan needed
to come with Mark and

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:58.160
James Baigent and travel
down to Dorset where the lawyer

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:01.760
was going to
give Andrew Scanlan this money.

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:03.040
And of course,
for Andrew Scanlan,

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.560
a sum of money of
five thousand pounds is

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:08.360
a massive amount of money.

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:11.160
VO: If the story is
true then the Baigents,

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:15.000
Andrew's half-brothers, are
likely to be the last people

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:17.200
to have seen him alive.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:26.080
VO: Detective
Superintendent Mark Birch:

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.880
has new suspects in his hunt
for missing

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:31.280
35-year-old Andrew Scanlan.

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:37.480
Andrew's half-brothers Mark
and James Baigent were seen

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:39.920
picking him up from
his home in Peterborough on

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:41.360
the night he disappeared.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:46.400
VO: Using number
plate recognition technology,

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:56.960
Mark and his team
are able to follow their path.

00:10:57.040 --> 00:11:00.680
Mark PTC:
We had tracked the car.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:01.920
What route did the car take?

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.080
And we knew Andrew had his
phone with him so we could

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:07.040
also overlap that
intelligence with

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.120
the intelligence from the car.

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.440
We knew that there'd
been some text messages

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:16.920
and some Voicemails sent...
and what was clearly obvious

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:18.960
is that the car,
instead of going into central

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:22.200
London as one of the text messages actually said-

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:23.600
what it had actually
done is travelled round

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:29.000
the M25 and then had
left the M25, heading towards,

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:32.920
and near by
the address of, James Baigent.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:37.480
VO: The route tracked by
the police stops well short

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:40.920
of Dorset, where the brothers had told Andrew he'd be

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:44.240
collecting a legacy
from their late mother.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:47.600
Nor does it take him
to London, dropped off by mates,

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:49.720
as suggested
in the text message.

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:53.320
Mark PTC: You can make
a supposition: did they forcibly

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:56.120
make him send that text
message and to try and put

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:59.000
his girlfriend off the scent?

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:01.040
But more importantly I think
they did it to try and put

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:01.960
the police off the scent.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:07.400
VO: Instead police
tracked the car to Aldershot,

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:09.800
32 miles south-west of London.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:17.120
Meanwhile, DCS Birch
and his team are exploring

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:21.320
why Andrew's brothers
may want to cause him harm.

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:24.440
They believe there's
a clue in the date he was taken.

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:26.400
Mark PTC: This
was the seventeenth of November.

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:30.560
Their mother died
on the eighteenth of October,

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.760
so one-month's
anniversary of her death.

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:39.440
VO: According to Andrew
Scanlan's girlfriend Louise,

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:42.960
the relationship between Andrew
and his brothers is fractured.

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:46.760
Mark PTC: Just shortly
after the death of their mother,

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:50.720
Mark Baigent had turned up at
the Dickens Road address and by

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:54.600
all accounts Mark Baigent
and Andrew Scanlan had a fight.

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.960
Mark Baigent was telling
Andrew Scanlan not to come

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.120
to their mother's funeral.

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:02.360
And there was a massive
amount of antagonism

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:07.880
and hatred between James and
Mark Baigent and Andrew Scanlan.

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:11.760
And that was based around
the fact that they believed

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:14.640
that Andrew Scanlan was
directly responsible for

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:15.440
their mother's death.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:18.480
Mark PTC: And the reason
they blamed him for

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:20.800
their mother's death
was Andrew was a drug addict,

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:24.200
he'd had various other
problems and she'd been there

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:25.760
to support Andrew.

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:29.080
And they felt that had
put an undue level of stress

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.160
upon her and had
led to her early death.

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:40.200
VO: The police investigation
soon reveals more bad blood

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:42.480
between the brothers.

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:45.480
Ten years earlier Mark Baigent
had been given a four-year

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:49.280
prison term for attempted
armed robbery and possession

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:50.520
of a firearm.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:54.640
Mark PTC: There was a huge
suspicion amongst the brothers

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.840
that Andrew had been responsible
for informing the police about

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:01.320
an armed
robbery some years earlier.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:04.960
So this hatred was all
the time being ramped up

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:07.200
so that as soon as
the mother was dead,

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.200
now they had no reason
for him to stay alive.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:11.840
They hated him.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:16.440
From that very moment
they were hatching a plan.

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:21.520
VO: Mark Birch: now has
a motive and a theory - that the

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:33.120
Baigents marked the one-month
anniversary of their mother's

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:37.400
death in the most brutal
way possible: abducting

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:41.040
and then killing
their hated half-brother.

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:46.120
Mark PTC: From the moment
their mother died I think Andrew

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:47.320
Scanlan was a dead man walking.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:53.960
VO: The Baigent brothers
were questioned early on in the

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:59.800
enquiry, when Andrew was still
presumed missing, not dead.

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:02.480
They claimed not
to have seen him.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:05.160
If they have murdered their
half-brother there's no

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:07.240
clue yet as to how or where.

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:13.160
But slowly the evidence stacks
up to support Birch's theory.

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:19.680
Mark PTC: So we now knew
roughly the route that Andrew

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:22.000
Scanlan had travelled
when he left Dickens Street

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:23.960
in Peterborough and
ended up round into Hampshire.

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:30.080
Now Mark and James Baigent
actually had denied

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:31.880
having anything
to do with him at this stage.

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:33.960
In fact, James had said
they hadn't gone round there.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:39.960
Suddenly we've got lies and
we had a motive in terms of

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:43.160
the hatred that was going on,
so at that stage it was becoming

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:45.000
increasingly obvious to me that
he was going to be dead ...

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:47.400
and we were looking for a body.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:50.080
The problem was we just
didn't know where the body was.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.360
VO: As the police dig deeper
it becomes evident that Mark

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:02.640
and James Baigent
did not act alone.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:05.840
Mark PTC: I then start
analysing all the telephones

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:09.720
that we've
got, and what became obvious,

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:13.520
there was a third
male Involved in this case.

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:15.160
And this
was a close friend of theirs,

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:16.920
a guy by
the name of Jeff Woods.

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:22.800
Jeff was a
tree surgeon by trade,

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:24.600
he had a van
with all the cutting material,

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:29.680
and he lived not too far away
from where James Baigent lived.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:35.560
VO: Woods and the Baigent
brothers have known each

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.320
other for years.

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:41.080
Mark PTC: All three of
them are Involved in war games,

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:43.560
they liked to go out
and dress up as soldiers

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:44.600
and all this sort of stuff.

00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:46.360
But they were really tight
as a group and got

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.120
on very well together.

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:51.160
And it suddenly became fairly
obvious that the three of

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:53.600
them were likely to have been
Involved in Andrew Scanlan's

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:56.160
disappearance
and ultimately death.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:17:01.400
VO: Now the police have three
prime suspects: brothers

00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:06.880
Mark and James Baigent
and their friend Jeff Woods.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.480
Mark PTC: So the next
plan for me is arrest.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:12.840
But it isn't just
a case of 'Right, that's it,

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:14.920
we're just going to go and
arrest' because I don't have

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.280
to arrest this second,
and what I wanted to do was

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:19.080
plan the arrest
so that all three of them

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:20.400
were arrested simultaneously.

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:25.360
VO: DCS Birch wants
to catch the men off-guard.

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:28.520
Mark PTC: We've got a group
of officers at each location to

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:30.440
carry out those arrests.

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:34.200
We've also got forensic staff
and we want to retrieve as much

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:37.560
trace evidence
from those scenes as possible.

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.920
We were looking to find trace
evidence of Andrew Scanlan's

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:47.520
body, or existence.

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:59.640
VO: The police make their
move in the early hours

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.400
of the morning.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:06.200
Mark Baigent, James Baigent
and Jeff Woods are arrested

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:10.920
on suspicion of murder.

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:16.840
As the men are taken
out the forensic teams move in.

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:26.200
Mark PTC: What became really quite apparent,

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:29.680
that all three of them had
researched heavily now to not

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:32.680
get caught on forensic evidence.

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:35.480
And we knew that by the
literature and the DVD's we'd

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:37.600
found at the addresses.

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:40.360
From NCIS,
CSI, American programmes.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.640
We had a witness statement
that identified that they were

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:49.920
seen cleaning
the Ford Escort that they

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:55.520
travelled round the M25
in with Andrew Scanlan.

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:57.920
And by cleaning it, they'd not
only cleaned it out properly,

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:00.200
but they'd wrapped sticky tape
round their hands and they'd

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:02.400
taped down the back seats
and they'd taped down

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:03.440
the interior of the car.

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:07.640
So they wanted to get rid
of any idea that he'd ever

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:10.000
been in that car,
either alive or dead.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:15.880
They'd planned this, in
their minds, quite meticulously.

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:20.800
They actually thought they were
going to get away with murder.

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:31.800
VO: The suspects are held
at Thorpe Wood Police Station

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:34.160
in Peterborough.

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:39.840
DCS Birch has ninety-six hours
to charge them or release them.

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:41.760
Mark PTC: The clock has
started and now we need to

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:43.280
start getting
on with the interviews.

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:47.840
We can put different
things that are being said

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:49.840
by each individual
to the other individuals.

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:56.080
It's quite a complex
strategized process.

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:59.640
VO: The three
men are questioned separately.

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:01.560
Mark PTC: They were
arrogant, they were confident,

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:04.760
they were nasty.

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:11.600
VO: And at first the
detectives make little headway.

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:13.560
Mark PTC: All three
of them just refused to give

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:15.760
us any explanation.

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:17.800
They were simply
brothers-in-arms.

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:19.360
They were not going to tell
the police anything

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:22.000
and I think all three of them
thought 'we stick to this story,

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:27.040
we're going to be home dry'.

00:20:30.960 --> 00:20:37.080
VO: As the interviews
continue in Peterborough,

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:40.760
house-to-house enquiries in
Hampshire start to bear fruit.

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:44.160
Mark PTC: We start to unearth
these bits of information

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:46.120
to put to them even further.

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:49.000
So for example, witnesses
had seen people trying

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:50.760
to clean the Escort.

00:20:50.800 --> 00:20:53.360
Whilst they were doing that,
seen nearby was a

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:54.680
tree surgeon's van.

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:58.640
And of course we know that
Jeff Woods was a tree surgeon.

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:05.280
VO: The witness statements
provide Mark Birch:

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:08.480
with vital ammunition
in the interview suites.

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:09.520
Mark PTC:
So when you're questioning,

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:12.840
what you're doing with each
question as you move forwards

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:15.920
is revealing what you know.

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:22.680
We would have gone back
time and time and time again.

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:24.440
It was hours
and hours of interviews.

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:28.600
VO: So far, all three men have
repeatedly refused to discuss

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:30.160
the murder with detectives.

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:37.080
But now, after two full days of
interview, one of them cracks.

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:41.280
Mark PTC: Suddenly out
of nowhere Jeff Woods decided

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:42.760
he wanted to talk to us.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:51.720
VO: Thirty-five-year-old Andrew Scanlan has been missing,

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:54.800
believed murdered,
for nearly two months.

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:58.800
The police have
three suspects under arrest,

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:02.440
two of them
Andrew's half-brothers.

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:04.880
All claim their innocence.

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:08.360
With forty-eight hours to go
before they must be released

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:12.600
one of them, tree surgeon
Jeff Woods, agrees to talk.

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:17.680
Mark PTC: He doesn't have
to be the Brain of Britain

00:22:22.560 --> 00:22:24.760
to work out as we're moving
on through our questioning

00:22:24.800 --> 00:22:28.520
over hours and hours and
hours that we know an awful lot.

00:22:28.600 --> 00:22:31.400
And that actually,
as it stands at the moment,

00:22:31.440 --> 00:22:36.200
he's going to be charged with
the murder of Andrew Scanlan.

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:40.200
And he had to think of a story
to get himself out of the frame.

00:22:40.240 --> 00:22:46.640
VO: Out of the blue,
Jeff Woods tells investigators

00:22:46.680 --> 00:22:54.000
he knows the whereabouts
of Andrew Scanlan's body.

00:22:54.080 --> 00:22:55.000
Mark PTC: Did it,
did it surprise us?

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:57.960
Yes, it did, because suddenly
out of nowhere - at quite

00:22:58.000 --> 00:22:59.960
a late stage in
our custody time-limit as well.

00:23:00.040 --> 00:23:01.560
That's another
thing that, you know,

00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:03.400
you need to understand
that we were getting towards

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:05.400
the end of the time
when we either had to charge

00:23:05.480 --> 00:23:09.160
or we had to release
them without charge.

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:11.640
But it's not uncommon
once you do get a,

00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:15.200
a complicity
of individuals engaged in a,

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:17.440
in something of this nature,
for one of them to try

00:23:17.480 --> 00:23:19.800
and protect themselves
and say they didn't do it.

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:24.360
What Jeff was telling
us, in real simple terms,

00:23:24.440 --> 00:23:27.160
was that he
didn't commit the murder.

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:29.360
All he did was assist
in getting rid of the body.

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:32.240
That the two guys,
the Baigent brothers,

00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:35.440
had killed Andrew Scanlan
and then on top of that he

00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:38.360
was quite prepared to
take us and show us where

00:23:38.400 --> 00:23:43.120
the body had
been deposited.

00:23:57.520 --> 00:24:00.200
- We're at Sandy Hill
Road and we're about to do

00:24:00.280 --> 00:24:03.560
a route walk with Jeff Woods.

00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:07.080
- OK, do you want to lead on?

00:24:07.160 --> 00:24:10.600
VO: Jeff has brought police
to the outskirts of Aldershot,

00:24:10.640 --> 00:24:12.840
one hundred and
twenty miles from Peterborough.

00:24:12.920 --> 00:24:16.680
Mark PTC: Just in the end
it was literally booked him

00:24:16.760 --> 00:24:19.760
out of custody and took
him to the location where he,

00:24:19.840 --> 00:24:20.760
where he wanted to go.

00:24:20.840 --> 00:24:24.160
He starts to
talk to the officers.

00:24:24.240 --> 00:24:26.440
We're video-recording it
so everything can be seen

00:24:26.480 --> 00:24:31.040
as being completely
above board and legitimate.

00:24:31.120 --> 00:24:33.440
[Jeff talking to
police officers]

00:25:03.400 --> 00:25:05.520
Mark PTC: We were actually
coming towards the end of

00:25:05.600 --> 00:25:07.560
our custody time limits.

00:25:07.600 --> 00:25:11.200
We've only got a short period of
time that we've got to then go

00:25:11.280 --> 00:25:15.120
out and find this body and then
do all the work that would need

00:25:15.200 --> 00:25:18.520
to be done around that.

00:25:18.600 --> 00:25:21.080
VO: If Jeff Woods knows
his custody deadline will

00:25:21.160 --> 00:25:26.640
soon expire, this could
be a deliberate delaying tactic.

00:25:26.680 --> 00:25:28.080
Mark PTC: Is
he telling us the truth?

00:25:28.160 --> 00:25:30.120
You know, suddenly he's out of
nowhere he wants to talk this.

00:25:30.200 --> 00:25:33.840
Is it a ruse to try and, er,
waste up a load of police time?

00:25:33.880 --> 00:25:37.440
- Right, I need
to get my bearings now.

00:25:37.520 --> 00:25:48.400
- Here, it's it's,
through here.

00:25:48.640 --> 00:25:50.200
Mark PTC: He was kind
of 'Yeah, I think it's here,

00:25:50.280 --> 00:25:53.200
I think it's there,
oh I'm not really sure it's

00:25:53.280 --> 00:25:55.200
somewhere up here,
it's somewhere round here'.

00:25:55.240 --> 00:25:57.680
'Cause if he was too sure
I think he was thinking

00:25:57.760 --> 00:25:59.240
well it's 'cause
we've all planned it together,

00:25:59.280 --> 00:26:01.280
the three of us planned this,
we always talked about

00:26:01.320 --> 00:26:03.160
where we're going
to put the body.

00:26:03.240 --> 00:26:06.800
We always talked about
where we're going to kill him.

00:26:07.720 --> 00:26:11.440
Jeff: Officer: If you can see, um, that, that hut,

00:26:11.520 --> 00:26:13.840
it might be
something like that hut inside.

00:26:13.920 --> 00:26:15.920
And that's what
you're looking for.

00:26:15.960 --> 00:26:18.560
A hut like that, um ...

00:26:18.600 --> 00:26:21.040
It's a bunker-like
complex is it?

00:26:21.120 --> 00:26:22.960
An old bunker?

00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:25.040
Yes.

00:26:25.120 --> 00:26:26.480
OK.

00:26:26.560 --> 00:26:32.360
An old bunker and you go
behind this, this bunker.

00:26:32.440 --> 00:26:33.440
I think I might
have come too far up,

00:26:33.520 --> 00:26:35.680
I think it
might be further down this way.

00:26:35.720 --> 00:26:38.080
VO: It begins to look
as if Jeff Woods may indeed

00:26:38.120 --> 00:26:41.400
be leading police
on a wild-goose chase.

00:26:41.480 --> 00:26:43.600
Jeff: No, it's
not further than that there.

00:26:43.680 --> 00:26:46.320
So it's from here this way.

00:26:46.400 --> 00:26:48.560
So it's in here somewhere.

00:26:54.560 --> 00:26:56.400
Mark PTC: So we get to
the vicinity of where he says

00:26:56.440 --> 00:26:59.320
the body may
or may not be.

00:26:59.400 --> 00:27:01.640
We don't know whether he's,
it's some trick to put

00:27:01.680 --> 00:27:04.800
us off the scent.

00:27:04.840 --> 00:27:06.120
Officer Jeff: I know I'm here. I'm definitely,

00:27:06.200 --> 00:27:06.880
definitely here.

00:27:06.960 --> 00:27:12.360
It's on the end
of this path and it's in here.

00:27:12.560 --> 00:27:15.600
OK, so when you walk in here
was there trees touching you

00:27:15.680 --> 00:27:16.440
or anything like that?

00:27:16.520 --> 00:27:17.880
Oh yeah, yeah...
There was trees touching you?

00:27:17.920 --> 00:27:21.080
I did say, remember I said
thick pine trees in the middle.

00:27:21.160 --> 00:27:21.920
Officer: Yes.

00:27:21.960 --> 00:27:24.240
So it's here but I need
to just ... if I can step In

00:27:24.320 --> 00:27:25.200
and have a look?

00:27:25.280 --> 00:27:26.000
Yes.

00:27:26.080 --> 00:27:27.080
I'm not going
to in, I won't go very far in.

00:27:27.160 --> 00:27:29.360
[Jeff searching]

00:27:35.840 --> 00:27:36.440
There's your hut, there.

00:27:36.520 --> 00:27:37.440
Oh yeah.

00:27:37.480 --> 00:27:38.960
There's you hut, bingo!

00:27:39.040 --> 00:27:40.240
Hang on.

00:27:40.280 --> 00:27:41.040
Hang on, hang on.

00:27:41.080 --> 00:27:43.080
Mark PTC: As soon as he points
out an area we can't have him

00:27:43.120 --> 00:27:48.240
trooping in there and trouncing
all over the area because all

00:27:48.320 --> 00:27:51.400
you're doing is contaminating it
with one of your suspects'

00:27:51.480 --> 00:27:53.520
DNA and trace evidence.

00:27:53.600 --> 00:27:55.000
Officer Jeff: So in
relation to the hut,

00:27:55.080 --> 00:27:57.760
we need to go round
the back of the hut.

00:27:57.840 --> 00:27:58.920
Yeah.

00:27:58.960 --> 00:27:59.920
Round the back.

00:27:59.960 --> 00:28:01.600
And how far behind
it is it there?

00:28:01.680 --> 00:28:03.520
Um... I, I'll
know by the floor.

00:28:03.600 --> 00:28:05.920
Right, OK.

00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:07.320
Well I think
I'll know by the floor.

00:28:07.400 --> 00:28:08.880
Like it may
remind...I did it...

00:28:08.960 --> 00:28:11.160
when I was here this was...

00:28:11.240 --> 00:28:12.960
I couldn't, I couldn't
see you from here so ...

00:28:13.040 --> 00:28:14.320
Yeah, from, from my point
of view what I want to try is

00:28:14.400 --> 00:28:17.240
actually take into a different,
from a different angle.

00:28:17.280 --> 00:28:20.520
So we know that, not the
angle you came in from before.

00:28:20.600 --> 00:28:22.920
Well if we walk towards
it and then I go right round it.

00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:25.080
What, what I was going to
suggest is there's a path down,

00:28:25.120 --> 00:28:26.960
you know that path there that
skirts round the edge of here?

00:28:27.040 --> 00:28:28.160
Yeah.

00:28:28.240 --> 00:28:29.840
I'm wondering if we can
go down that path a little bit

00:28:29.920 --> 00:28:31.360
and then look back
across first of all,

00:28:31.400 --> 00:28:33.000
before we go ... clean route.

00:28:33.080 --> 00:28:36.160
So basically
we just keep a clean route, OK?

00:28:36.200 --> 00:28:38.320
No, no, no, I understand
what you're saying.

00:28:38.400 --> 00:28:40.000
Yeah, that's fine,
I understand.

00:28:40.080 --> 00:28:41.440
Mark PTC: We finally get
to a point where he points

00:28:41.480 --> 00:28:43.920
out 'That's where he is,
that's where I think it is'.

00:28:53.960 --> 00:28:55.080
OK, just step, step back again.

00:28:56.160 --> 00:28:58.120
That's it.

00:28:58.160 --> 00:29:01.640
It's either
that one, or that one there.

00:29:01.720 --> 00:29:02.960
There are two ...

00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:04.240
That area there?

00:29:04.320 --> 00:29:05.400
Or the one in front.

00:29:05.480 --> 00:29:06.280
It's either one of those or...

00:29:06.360 --> 00:29:07.440
That one or there?

00:29:07.520 --> 00:29:08.360
Yes.

00:29:08.400 --> 00:29:09.400
Mark PTC: So of course, the
minute he points it out we've

00:29:09.440 --> 00:29:11.600
then got to go in with
a forensic team and recover

00:29:11.680 --> 00:29:16.080
that scene, or search
that scene as best we can.

00:29:16.160 --> 00:29:19.200
VO: While Jeff Woods is
returned to custody the forensic

00:29:19.240 --> 00:29:21.960
specialists move in.

00:29:22.040 --> 00:29:27.000
Mark PTC: So a forensic
team went into the clearing.

00:29:27.080 --> 00:29:29.560
There was an
outbuilding that was nearby,

00:29:29.640 --> 00:29:31.600
it looked like
a bunker of some sort.

00:29:31.680 --> 00:29:34.360
And then just to the
right there was a shallow grave,

00:29:34.440 --> 00:29:36.600
just a slight
indentation shallow grave.

00:29:36.680 --> 00:29:41.960
Mark PTC: What actually
transpired was it was

00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:44.000
two shallow graves.

00:29:47.120 --> 00:29:49.920
And you had the torso,
the main part of the body

00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:52.000
in one part
of the shallow grave.

00:29:55.360 --> 00:29:59.840
Literally a matter of a couple
of feet away was the severed

00:29:59.880 --> 00:30:03.000
head and hands of Andrew
Scanlan in a separate grave.

00:30:11.360 --> 00:30:13.760
VO: The body
of missing 35-year-old Andrew

00:30:13.840 --> 00:30:18.600
Scanlan has been discovered
- dismembered and lying in two

00:30:18.640 --> 00:30:22.640
shallow graves
on the outskirts of Aldershot.

00:30:22.720 --> 00:30:26.480
For DCS Birch,
dreadful as the discovery is,

00:30:26.560 --> 00:30:30.280
there's some comfort in knowing
Andrew has been found at last.

00:30:30.320 --> 00:30:33.000
Mark PTC: There's a feeling
of achieving what you set

00:30:33.080 --> 00:30:34.440
out to achieve.

00:30:34.520 --> 00:30:37.040
I felt really proud
of my team, I felt really proud

00:30:37.120 --> 00:30:38.040
of the investigation.

00:30:38.120 --> 00:30:44.280
I can't say I took any
like huge elation out of it

00:30:44.360 --> 00:30:45.600
'cause it's not
like that for me.

00:30:45.680 --> 00:30:49.200
It was a professional outcome.

00:30:49.240 --> 00:30:56.480
I felt really sorry for the
guy who died, Andrew Scanlan.

00:31:01.600 --> 00:31:02.480
Mark PTC: It's all
about recovering

00:31:02.520 --> 00:31:04.880
the body with dignity.

00:31:04.920 --> 00:31:06.440
That's, you know,
that's a really big issue,

00:31:06.480 --> 00:31:07.360
believe it or not.

00:31:07.440 --> 00:31:09.560
But recovering every
evidential opportunity

00:31:09.640 --> 00:31:12.080
you can get 'cause you'll
get one bite at this.

00:31:12.120 --> 00:31:13.560
Once you've done that,
if you've lost anything

00:31:13.640 --> 00:31:23.400
in the recovery stage, you're
never going to have another go.

00:31:23.440 --> 00:31:25.640
Mark PTC: Just recovering
the body will take hours

00:31:25.720 --> 00:31:28.040
and hours and hours
and hours - days actually.

00:31:28.120 --> 00:31:30.240
Sometimes you won't remove a
body in a circumstance

00:31:30.320 --> 00:31:33.960
like that for
twenty-four, thirty-six hours.

00:31:35.520 --> 00:31:39.600
VO: One puzzle for Mark Birch:
and his team is why Andrew's

00:31:39.680 --> 00:31:44.440
killers have
buried his body as they have.

00:31:47.760 --> 00:31:50.280
Mark PTC: If you were going
to sever the head and the hands

00:31:50.360 --> 00:31:53.520
because you were thinking
about maybe dental records

00:31:53.560 --> 00:31:56.800
and fingerprint removal, well
you wouldn't put them in a

00:31:56.840 --> 00:31:59.800
grave immediately adjacent
to where you put the body.

00:31:59.840 --> 00:32:04.400
And my assumption is that I
think that they buried him in

00:32:04.440 --> 00:32:06.880
a shallow grave in the dark -
and it is pitch-dark -

00:32:06.960 --> 00:32:09.880
and then probably gone
back a day or two later

00:32:09.920 --> 00:32:11.240
and there's probably
something sticking out

00:32:11.280 --> 00:32:12.880
of the ground when
rigamortis maybe has

00:32:12.920 --> 00:32:14.920
set in,
or something has happened.

00:32:14.960 --> 00:32:18.880
It looks as though that
the decapitation and the hand

00:32:18.920 --> 00:32:22.160
removal was simply to
cover the body up and bury

00:32:22.240 --> 00:32:27.360
the body better.

00:32:27.400 --> 00:32:29.320
News presenter: The body
was found near a site where

00:32:29.400 --> 00:32:32.400
the three accused
men played war games together.

00:32:32.480 --> 00:32:35.840
The Baigent brothers came
here, to Andrew Scanlan's house,

00:32:35.880 --> 00:32:39.040
and enticed him into their car
by claiming they all needed

00:32:39.120 --> 00:32:42.480
to go to Dorset to sort
out their late mother's Will.

00:32:42.520 --> 00:32:45.520
Instead, it's said, they
drove him to Hampshire where

00:32:45.600 --> 00:32:47.480
he was beaten
and stabbed to death.

00:32:47.520 --> 00:32:51.680
VO: Now Andrew's
body has been found,

00:32:51.720 --> 00:32:54.880
DCS Birch hopes it will
offer up the evidence he needs

00:32:54.960 --> 00:32:57.480
to charge all
three men with his murder.

00:33:00.160 --> 00:33:06.280
VO: The post-mortem
will be critical.

00:33:07.920 --> 00:33:10.760
Mark PTC: The forensic
pathologists in our country

00:33:10.840 --> 00:33:11.880
are absolutely brilliant.

00:33:11.960 --> 00:33:14.200
It's not unusual to take
ten, twelve hours to carry

00:33:14.240 --> 00:33:15.440
out a forensic post-mortem.

00:33:15.480 --> 00:33:19.160
You know, the post-mortem
examination is absolutely

00:33:19.240 --> 00:33:22.160
carried out with
infinite detail.

00:33:22.240 --> 00:33:26.680
VO: Andrew's bruised
and dismembered body reveals

00:33:26.720 --> 00:33:30.720
the extent of the violence
inflicted on him by his killers.

00:33:30.760 --> 00:33:34.160
Mark PTC: The injuries that
he had were two stab wounds

00:33:34.240 --> 00:33:35.880
to his body,
and they didn't kill him.

00:33:35.960 --> 00:33:41.680
He's got bruising all over
his body consistent with

00:33:41.760 --> 00:33:44.080
being beaten
with a baseball bat.

00:33:44.160 --> 00:33:47.440
He's been
tortured pretty much.

00:33:58.360 --> 00:34:00.080
Mark PTC: You know they've,
they've given him a

00:34:00.120 --> 00:34:01.240
real good hiding.

00:34:01.320 --> 00:34:06.040
And then
they strangled him.

00:34:06.120 --> 00:34:07.560
Mark PTC: Dragged his
body up the hill,

00:34:07.640 --> 00:34:11.960
dragged him into the woods,
dug a shallow grave

00:34:12.000 --> 00:34:14.200
and buried him
in a shallow grave.

00:34:14.280 --> 00:34:18.600
But there was no definitive
cause of death in this case.

00:34:18.640 --> 00:34:23.160
They wanted to make
him hurt before they killed him.

00:34:23.240 --> 00:34:29.520
Mark PTC: The level of violence
was beyond anything I'd ever

00:34:29.600 --> 00:34:31.600
dealt with before.

00:34:33.120 --> 00:34:39.080
The, the sheer hatred and
the sheer vehement wish to, to,

00:34:39.160 --> 00:34:43.520
to kill him and to put him
in pain and be rid of him

00:34:43.600 --> 00:34:44.680
shone through all the way.

00:34:44.760 --> 00:34:49.760
If you think what Andrew
Scanlan must have been going

00:34:51.760 --> 00:34:55.200
through for that last
fifteen minutes to half an hour,

00:34:55.280 --> 00:34:57.080
he must
have been absolutely terrified.

00:35:01.720 --> 00:35:05.160
VO: DCS Birch still needs
forensic proof that the Baigent

00:35:05.240 --> 00:35:08.360
brothers and Jeff Woods
are together responsible

00:35:08.440 --> 00:35:11.360
for Andrew's murder.

00:35:12.160 --> 00:35:15.600
After hours of painstaking work
the pathologist delivers it.

00:35:18.760 --> 00:35:23.040
Mark PTC: We found a small
shard in the spine of Andrew

00:35:23.080 --> 00:35:29.320
Scanlan that potentially matched
a piece of metal, or an axe,

00:35:29.400 --> 00:35:31.800
that was found at James
Baigent's house and the paint

00:35:31.880 --> 00:35:33.480
that was on there
was a potential match.

00:35:38.480 --> 00:35:41.760
We found fibres in the car
that were belonging to Andrew

00:35:41.840 --> 00:35:44.760
Scanlan so we could positively
not only put him into the car

00:35:44.840 --> 00:35:52.400
by witness evidence
but also by trace evidence.

00:35:56.800 --> 00:35:58.240
Mark PTC: There was a pair
of shoes found at Jeff Woods's

00:35:58.280 --> 00:36:00.840
address that upon
examination had traces

00:36:00.920 --> 00:36:02.480
of Andrew Scanlan's blood.

00:36:02.520 --> 00:36:08.480
And there were also fibres
found on other items of clothing

00:36:08.520 --> 00:36:14.840
that would match between the
individuals and Andrew Scanlan.

00:36:14.920 --> 00:36:18.120
Mark PTC: We had
Jeff Woods telling us the story,

00:36:18.160 --> 00:36:21.560
we had the body found where
he said the body was found.

00:36:21.600 --> 00:36:23.960
All wrapped up together
you've got a really strong

00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:25.120
prosecution case.

00:36:25.200 --> 00:36:29.600
And that's
without witness testimony.

00:36:31.320 --> 00:36:34.640
VO: What witness statements
do soon reveal is

00:36:34.680 --> 00:36:37.360
the wider Involvement
of the Baigent family.

00:36:37.440 --> 00:36:41.200
Mark PTC: We
had the wife of James Baigent,

00:36:41.280 --> 00:36:45.920
Charlotte Baigent,
telling people at a party,

00:36:45.960 --> 00:36:49.160
a group of individuals,
that they'd been Involved

00:36:49.240 --> 00:36:51.360
in the murder of Andrew Scanlan.

00:36:51.440 --> 00:36:53.600
In fact she went
a lot further, she,

00:36:53.680 --> 00:36:55.800
the version she was telling
was that they'd done a

00:36:55.880 --> 00:36:59.960
lot more hideous things to the
body than actually had occurred.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:04.000
She was basically saying, you
know ... my family are murderers

00:37:04.040 --> 00:37:07.440
and if you're not careful
they're going to murder you.

00:37:07.480 --> 00:37:09.840
She assisted them in
the clean-up exercise,

00:37:09.880 --> 00:37:12.440
she got rid of their
clothing, she got rid of,

00:37:12.480 --> 00:37:16.120
um, evidence in the case
and she tried to lead us astray.

00:37:16.160 --> 00:37:19.680
So witness testimony
also became really significant

00:37:19.720 --> 00:37:21.320
in this case.

00:37:24.960 --> 00:37:27.680
VO: DCS Mark Birch: now
has enough evidence to send

00:37:27.760 --> 00:37:29.600
his three suspects to trial.

00:37:29.680 --> 00:37:33.120
Mark PTC: All three of the
men were charged with murder,

00:37:33.200 --> 00:37:35.720
remanded into custody,
and then some months later

00:37:35.800 --> 00:37:38.000
we got a trial with
the three of them for murder.

00:37:44.160 --> 00:37:46.680
VO: As the trial starts
the relationship between

00:37:46.760 --> 00:37:49.560
the accused changes rapidly.

00:37:49.640 --> 00:37:54.560
Once a band of brothers, now
they're turning on each other.

00:37:54.640 --> 00:37:57.280
Mark PTC: There is a term
called a 'cut-throat defence'.

00:37:57.360 --> 00:38:00.760
It became a situation where
these three guys who'd been

00:38:00.840 --> 00:38:03.280
tight as anything,
who'd been really close,

00:38:03.360 --> 00:38:07.800
suddenly you had Jeff
saying, 'You two killed him,

00:38:07.840 --> 00:38:09.040
all I did was help.

00:38:09.080 --> 00:38:11.360
I didn't kill him, I had
nothing to do with the murder'.

00:38:11.440 --> 00:38:13.960
And then on the counter-argument
was that you had

00:38:14.040 --> 00:38:16.120
the two brothers saying,
'Well this didn't happen,

00:38:16.200 --> 00:38:18.120
we were just going to give
him a beating because we didn't

00:38:18.200 --> 00:38:20.040
like him, Jeff you killed him'.

00:38:20.080 --> 00:38:25.240
VO: The trial runs for seven
weeks at Cambridge Crown Court

00:38:25.320 --> 00:38:28.800
before the jury reaches
its verdict in February 2008.

00:38:28.880 --> 00:38:32.520
Mark PTC: The verdict was
a unanimous decision by

00:38:32.560 --> 00:38:34.480
the jury who
didn't believe any of it.

00:38:34.560 --> 00:38:37.440
Thought all three of the men
were complicit in the murder

00:38:37.520 --> 00:38:40.600
of Andrew Scanlan and found
all three men guilty of murder.

00:38:40.680 --> 00:38:46.960
In sentencing, the judge
said the murder showed

00:38:47.040 --> 00:38:49.160
a degree of
pre-meditation and planning.

00:38:49.240 --> 00:38:52.560
Andrew Scanlan was kidnapped,
humiliated in the minutes

00:38:52.640 --> 00:38:56.320
before he died, his body
dismembered and then concealed.

00:38:56.360 --> 00:38:57.960
All three men
were jailed for life.

00:38:58.040 --> 00:39:02.480
Journalist PTC: James Baigent,
who the judge said was

00:39:02.560 --> 00:39:05.560
the plot's ringleader,
will spend a minimum of

00:39:05.640 --> 00:39:07.120
twenty-four years in prison.

00:39:07.160 --> 00:39:10.240
His brother Mark
a minimum of twenty-two years,

00:39:10.320 --> 00:39:14.080
and Jeff Woods who assisted in
the murder and the dismemberment

00:39:14.160 --> 00:39:15.720
a minimum of twenty years.

00:39:15.800 --> 00:39:19.200
The judge said he had no
doubt the two brothers had

00:39:19.240 --> 00:39:22.800
used episodes of CSI
to try and cover their tracks

00:39:22.880 --> 00:39:26.080
and he praised the real
police and forensic service

00:39:26.160 --> 00:39:28.080
for bringing the three
of them to justice.

00:39:28.160 --> 00:39:32.480
VO: Charlotte Baigent
is convicted of assisting her

00:39:32.520 --> 00:39:36.120
husband and brother-in-law
and sentenced to twelve months.

00:39:46.360 --> 00:39:48.640
Mark PTC: I was there for
the verdict and the sentencing.

00:39:48.720 --> 00:39:52.520
I felt really proud of my
team, I felt really proud of

00:39:52.600 --> 00:39:54.880
the investigation, I felt really, really proud

00:39:54.960 --> 00:39:56.640
of everyone's
Involvement in this case.

00:39:56.680 --> 00:40:03.200
I think the sibling hatred,
that was the thing that was

00:40:03.280 --> 00:40:07.640
really something I'd
never come across to that extent

00:40:07.720 --> 00:40:09.640
and you kind of think
that siblings shouldn't behave

00:40:09.720 --> 00:40:11.040
like that to one another.

00:40:11.120 --> 00:40:13.480
And so that was the thing that
really stuck in my mind about

00:40:13.560 --> 00:40:15.840
this, this murder
and, and how they behaved.

00:40:15.920 --> 00:40:19.600
It was that sheer callousness,
that sheer cold-bloodedness

00:40:19.680 --> 00:40:21.440
towards their
own flesh and blood.

00:40:21.520 --> 00:40:25.840
Mark PTC: They could have just
disassociated themselves

00:40:25.920 --> 00:40:28.960
and gone off and li ... lived
a happy life but something

00:40:29.040 --> 00:40:32.480
inside them gee'd them up that
they had to do it for their

00:40:32.520 --> 00:40:37.520
own egotistical reasons.

00:40:45.360 --> 00:40:47.760
VO: Peter Cottrell,
Andrew's friend,

00:40:47.840 --> 00:40:49.880
was there on the night
Andrew was taken away by his

00:40:49.960 --> 00:40:55.680
half-brothers, supposedly
to claim his inheritance.

00:40:55.760 --> 00:40:58.200
Peter Cottrell PTC: No way I,
at that point when his brothers

00:40:58.240 --> 00:41:01.040
turned up that I thought it,
they were going to do what

00:41:01.120 --> 00:41:02.440
they did to him.

00:41:02.480 --> 00:41:05.560
It, it makes me sick to
the stomach thinking about that.

00:41:05.640 --> 00:41:09.920
It's just so, so dark.

00:41:10.000 --> 00:41:14.600
It's such a dark crime.

00:41:14.680 --> 00:41:17.200
Peter PTC: The fact that
they were related to Andrew

00:41:17.280 --> 00:41:24.480
is absolutely shocking because
Andrew wouldn't hurt anybody.

00:41:24.560 --> 00:41:25.600
He, he wasn't that way.

00:41:25.640 --> 00:41:30.160
I never seen him
fall out with anyone.

00:41:30.240 --> 00:41:33.480
All, all I saw was kindness
and, and happiness with Andrew,

00:41:33.560 --> 00:41:36.240
that's, that's who he was.

00:41:36.280 --> 00:41:41.280
Never an angry person,
always happy-go-lucky.

00:41:41.360 --> 00:41:42.720
I wish he was still here.

00:41:46.400 --> 00:41:49.520
VO: Today Andrew
Scanlan's resting place

00:41:49.560 --> 00:41:53.880
is an unmarked grave.

00:41:53.960 --> 00:41:57.520
Mark PTC: It's human life,
as simple as that, you know.

00:41:57.600 --> 00:42:01.280
We've got the right to life
and ultimately no one has

00:42:01.360 --> 00:42:04.640
got the right
to take that life away from you.

00:42:04.720 --> 00:42:07.960
Andrew Scanlan might not have
been an upstanding member

00:42:08.040 --> 00:42:09.520
of the public,
he might have been a low-level

00:42:09.600 --> 00:42:12.520
criminal and he was
estranged from his family,

00:42:12.600 --> 00:42:16.320
and whatever he was
he didn't deserve to be

00:42:16.400 --> 00:42:17.440
a victim of murder.

00:42:19.560 --> 00:42:21.160
He didn't deserve
what happened to him.

